# .github/docs-map — surfaces that must move with the code they describe
#
# Read by scripts/ci/check-docs-sync.sh. One entry per line:
#
#   <glob matching changed paths>    <surface that must change too>
#
# The glob is matched against each changed path with shell pattern matching, so
# `*` does not stop at a "/" — write `plugins/*/skills/*` rather than relying on
# a stricter globstar.
#
# Keep this table SMALL. Every entry here is a rule that will one day fire on a
# change it should not, and a check that is usually wrong gets switched off
# within a week — at which point it protects nothing. Add an entry when a real
# omission has happened, not when one seems imaginable. Remove an entry that
# turns out to be noise rather than working around it in pull request bodies.
#
# Deliberately absent: README.md. Almost no code change needs it, so requiring
# it would be wrong far more often than right. It lives in the pull request
# template instead, where it costs a glance rather than a red build.

